# Workspace Entry

Project-local lite workflow entrypoints:

- Stage advance: `pwsh -File .assistant\entry\advance-stage.ps1 -TaskId <task-id>` (Codex-only defaults; add `-Tool <claudecode|codex>` only to switch backend)
- Artifact validation: `pwsh -File .assistant\entry\validate-lite-artifacts.ps1 -TaskId <task-id>`
- New task routing: keep `resume-current / switch-existing / new-task / inbox-first` first; when the result is `new-task`, choose `mode: quick | workflow | ask`.

These shims delegate to the managed harness repo scripts and always use the installed shared vault:

- Repo root: `{REPO_ROOT}`
- Vault root: `{VAULT_PATH}`

`TEST -> DONE` also omits `-Tool`; non-DONE stages use the workflow descriptor when no explicit backend is passed.

Mode routing: `quick` only when all true: scope and acceptance are clear, risk is low, the task can finish and be verified in the current conversation, and the user did not ask for durable notes / review / test / planning. Use `workflow` when any of these is true: the user asks for workflow / durable notes / review / test / planning, the change touches entry protocol, scripts, templates, validators, multiple modules, high-risk paths, or durable decisions/artifacts. Use `ask` as Deep Clarification Mode when missing answers block intent, scope, acceptance criteria, constraints, risk, affected area, output format, or route choice. Ask mode is an iterative blocking clarification gate: ask one highest-value question at a time by default, reassess after each answer, and Remain in ask until all blocking uncertainties are resolved. Clarification-family triggers such as `需求澄清` / `需求确认` / `拷问` / `头脑风暴` / `方案压力测试` / `边界确认` enter existing `PLAN -> Clarification` when a development task needs durable decisions.

For development tasks, entry-router is the default first hop. Do not invoke other workflow skills before routing; after routing, load only the context required by the selected mode.

Clarification trigger rule: unresolved PLAN acceptance, non-goals, impact, rollback/compatibility, or implementation path that cannot guide IMPLEMENT also enters the Clarification protocol.

Clarification ledger rule: answer code/doc-discoverable questions first, keep the base Clarification fields, ask remaining user decisions one at a time with a recommended answer, and keep `User Confirmation` draft while any `clarification_ledger` item is `decision: pending`.

Stage principle routing: use these as cognitive lenses only, not a new five-turn workflow: Entry/Clarification=Socrates, PLAN=Osborn/Hegel/First Principles/Occam, PLAN_REVIEW=Hegel+Bayes, IMPLEMENT=Ponytail/surgical change, CODE_REVIEW=Feynman, TEST=Bayes, revise=Debono value preservation.

Stage Discipline Matrix: the managed harness repo keeps the full advisory matrix at `docs/工作流/stage-discipline-matrix.md`; load it only when the task requires stage-discipline clarification or stage-behavior review.

Implementation rule: 新功能开发或功能修改以当前需求和业务正确性为准；不要为了兼容旧测试、旧快照或过期断言而保留或恢复旧行为。若旧测试与新需求冲突，应更新或删除旧测试并说明原因；只有用户明确要求历史兼容时才保留旧测试兼容。

Lazy loading:

- `quick`: load only entry rules, user preferences / necessary config, and the directly relevant skill or reference.
- `workflow`: load `entry-router`, `orchestrator`, then exactly one current-stage skill (`plan`, `review`, `implement`, or `test`).
- `resume-current` / `switch-existing`: load existing runtime files only if present (`.assistant\运行时\恢复索引.md`, `.assistant\运行时\当前任务.md`, `运行时\tasks\<task-id>.md`), then the current-stage skill; missing runtime files mean no active recorded state.
- `ask`: do not load workflow stage skills; do not enter quick, workflow, PLAN, IMPLEMENT, or later stages; do not create `docs/tasks/{task_id}/`, edit code, or initialize providers. Remain in ask until all blocking uncertainties are resolved.
- Do not bulk-load all skills, all historical `docs/tasks/*`, Claude compatibility skills, or `workflow-team` unless an explicit backend, stage, or team-mode trigger requires it.

Ask exit criteria: ask cannot exit until the agent can state User goal, Success / acceptance criteria, In scope, Out of scope / non-goals, Affected area, Constraints, Risk level, Expected output, Recommended route: quick or workflow, and Why this route is safe. If any item is materially unknown and affects the work, remain in ask.

Ask response format: state why you remain in ask, list what is already understood, name the current blocker, ask one high-value question, include a recommended default answer when useful, and say you will reassess quick vs workflow after confirmation.
